+// CHANCE. A per-step probability, 0..100 (clamped), decided once per LANDING:
+// whenever a clock edge or a reset puts the playhead on a step. A rest rolls
+// nothing. A hit at chance 100 plays and rolls nothing, a hit at chance 0 is
+// silent and rolls nothing, and any other hit makes exactly one
+// rng.percent() call and plays when the result is below `chance`. The verdict
+// holds for the whole stay: a hit that lost its roll is a rest until the
+// playhead moves (no strike, GATE low on every sample, so the gate gap of a
+// later reset sees it low too), and idle samples never re-roll. Nothing else
+// touches the generator — not load(), not idle samples, not rests — so a
+// seeded Rng replays the same verdicts for the same clock/reset sequence.
+// The pattern table is never changed by a lost roll. The six-argument
+// process() is chance 100 and never consumes the generator.
+//
